# CO & Combustion Efficiency Implementation Plan

## Goal Description
Implement Carbon Monoxide (CO) emissions tracking for Stationary Combustion and Flaring processes to allow for the quantification of **Combustion Efficiency (CE)**.

**Formula:**
$$ CE (\%) = \frac{n_{CO2}}{n_{CO2} + n_{CO}} \times 100 $$
Where $n$ represents moles of the substance.
- $MW_{CO2} = 44.01 \text{ g/mol}$
- $MW_{CO} = 28.01 \text{ g/mol}$

## User Review Required
> [!NOTE]
> This change introduces a new "Specific CO Factor" input. If left blank, CO emissions will be 0, resulting in 100% calculated efficiency (ideal combustion).

## Proposed Changes

### 1. Data Layer ([emission-factors.js](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/h/public/emission-factors.js))
- Update `API_FACTORS` to include [co](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/h/public/toast.js#61-75) factors where available (default to placeholders or usage-based).
